hpc:Container a owl:Class .
hpc:Cluster a owl:Class .

hpc:name a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Container ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

hpc:index a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Container ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:memory a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Resource .

hpc:used a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Memory ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:allocated a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Memory ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:cpus a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Resource .

hpc:count a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Cpus ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:used a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Cpus ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:sockets a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Resource .

hpc:cores a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf hpc:Resource .

hpc:index a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Sockets ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer .

hpc:status a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain hpc:Cores ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .
```

This ontology fragment describes the classes `Container` and `Cluster`, and their properties such as `name`, `index`, `memory`, `used`, `allocated`, `cpus`, `count`, `used`, `sockets`, `cores`, `index`, and `status`. The properties are defined as datatype properties with their domains and ranges specified. The `Resource` class is used as a superclass for `Memory`, `Cpus`, and `Sockets`.
